+      # SPEC HEADER VERSION GATE (#1192) — tag-push path only. The ruling on
+      # #1192 (option a, `stamp`) has the release write the tag being cut into
+      # spec/brief-v1.md's `Describes reference implementation:` header, the
+      # same way it stamps the plugin manifest; check-spec-header-version.sh
+      # is the proof the stamp ran. A pushed tag can never be re-pointed, so on
+      # that path the tagged tree must already carry the tag — refuse it HERE,
+      # before the human approval, exactly as the manifest gate above does. On
+      # the dispatch path the tree is not stamped yet (`release` stamps it
+      # before tagging), so the proof runs there, right after the stamp.
+      - name: Release gate — refuse a pushed tag whose spec/brief-v1.md header names another version
+        if: github.event_name == 'push'
