+            # POST-CUT SPEC HEADER BUMP (#1192), in the same commit and under the
+            # same floor rule as the manifest bump above: leave the default
+            # branch's spec/brief-v1.md header on the next patch version, so the
+            # next dispatch of that version finds it already stamped; a header a
+            # human already moved ABOVE the cut is left alone. A header the stamp
+            # cannot read or rewrite fails the roll (the stamp exits 2) rather
